cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "dseams-plumed: the d-SEAMS topological ice score as a PLUMED action"
abstract: >-
  DSEAMS_CAGES is a PLUMED Colvar that scores the d-SEAMS topological ice
  state of a group of oxygen atoms every frame: the mutual/union
  four-nearest-neighbour graphs, primitive six-membered rings and seeded
  hexagonal/double-diamond cage assignment (nice, nmax, nclus, nic, nih,
  nmixed), CHILL+ on the cutoff graph (chillice, chillmax,
  chillinterfacial), the six-ring census (sixrings), ion brine rejection
  against the water assignment (nionice, nionfront, nionliq), local
  topology-key classification and LIBRARY naming (nclasses, nnamed),
  ring-size SIGNATURE cage counting (ncages) and guest occupancy
  (noccupied, nmultiple, nfreeguest). Every count carries no derivatives
  and feeds PRINT, COMMITTOR or other PLUMED analysis actions. Atom
  positions come from the host MD engine through PLUMED
  (ATOMS/IONS/GUESTS); the only file this action reads is a plain-text
  LIBRARY of topology keys. The linked seams-core engine optionally reads
  PDB/GRO/DCD (chemfiles) and .con (readcon-core) for its own CLI and
  front ends; this module exports dseams_plumed_has_chemfiles() and
  dseams_plumed_has_readcon() to report that support, but does not read
  structure files itself.
